Sharp Moment Stability of Brenier Maps
Lean formalization and publication packaging, 2026.

Includes source adapted from OpenAI math, https://github.com/openai/math,
commit fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb, under lean/vendor/openai/.
The original Apache-2.0 license is preserved in lean/vendor/openai/LICENSE.

The files under lean/vendor/openai/ are modified versions of the files of
lean/OAI/Analysis/Brenier/ in that repository. The changes are:
- every file has a Lean module header (module, public import, exposed public
  section) in place of its plain imports;
- the bodies of Basic, Atomic, Optimality and Wasserstein are compiled together
  in the added file TransportCore.lean, which uses targeted Mathlib imports in
  place of the omnibus import; their original paths are re-export wrappers that
  also keep the omnibus Mathlib import for the modules that depend on them;
- in Quantiles.lean the import precedes the leading comment block, as the
  module header requires;
- in PrefixSections.lean the definition `scalarBlock` is public instead of
  private, because it occurs in the body of an exposed public definition.
The mathematical statements and proof bodies are retained. The file list, the
SHA-256 of each included file and the same list of changes are recorded in
lean/VENDOR.json.

lean/BrenierMoment/ contains this project's formalization. Its statement
vocabulary in lean/BrenierMoment/Presentation/Model.lean follows the definitions
of OAI.Problem358 in OpenAI math.
The complete generated Lean4Web edition includes the adapted sources and
documents its packaging changes in its header and lean4web/sources.json.

The repository layout follows KitaKen1/bapat-lal-q-permanent-lean.
